{"decision":"edit","issues":[{"quote":"holding several motionless objects","problem":"This is an absolute stillness claim; the images show no clear movement but do not prove the objects are motionless."},{"quote":"A thin vertical pole shadow and a small device shadow fall across the lower-center of the frame","problem":"The device shadow is positioned toward the lower right, not the lower center, and 'the frame' is an annotation phrase."},{"quote":"every object holds its exact position and orientation without any visible translation, rotation, or occlusion","problem":"This is an unsupported absolute claim; the visible evidence supports only that the objects appear fixed with no clear translation or rotation."},{"quote":"The whole scene is brightly lit","problem":"The scene includes dark wet-sand patches and a dim interval, so 'whole scene' is too broad."},{"quote":"through the final frame","problem":"'Frame' is an annotation phrase and should be replaced with a direct visual reference."}],"caption":"The video captures a mostly static overhead view of a flat sandy surface holding several objects. A white plastic basin rests in a dark wet-sand patch on the left, while a short brown cylinder lies diagonally near the center beside an upright red-and-black marker.

On the right, a second dark wet-sand patch cradles a tangled pile of brightly colored thin sticks together with a green spoon-shaped item. A thin vertical pole shadow crosses the lower center, and a small device shadow sits at the lower right. The scene is brightly lit in these intervals, so the shadows read clearly against the pale sand, and the objects appear fixed in place and orientation, with no clear translation or rotation.

The visible change is then a temporary dip in illumination. The scene darkens noticeably and the pole and device shadows become faint, while the basin, cylinder, marker, and stick pile remain in place. After this dim interval the lighting returns to the brighter state, the shadows reappear, and the layout stays unchanged through the final view.","length_note":""}
